Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 9, lines 21-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 9, lines 21-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 9, lines 43-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 9, lines 43-47"}]}],"caption":"EPA v. Calumet Shreveport Refining, L.L.C.","case_history":[{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T20:06:14.651108Z","explanation":"An official oral-argument transcript was verified.","status":"argued"},{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T20:06:14.682828Z","explanation":"An official oral-argument transcript was verified.","status":"argued"},{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T23:55:45.291667Z","explanation":"An official Court opinion was verified.","status":"decided"}],"case_status":"decided","dek":"The dispute centers on whether a refinery must file its challenge in Washington, D.C., or in a local court.","dek_sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 110, lines 29-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 110, lines 29-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 50, lines 29-33","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 50, lines 29-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 35-37","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 35-37"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 72, lines 27-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 72, lines 27-21"}],"dispositions":[],"latest_court_document_date":"2025-03-25T00:00:00Z","maturity":"post_opinion","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2024","official_disposition_urls":["https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/24pdf/605us2r50_g2hk.pdf"],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/23-1229.html","primary_docket":"23-1229","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T15:47:43.049660Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":1},{"correction_note":"Migrated to the dated official Court activity contract without model use.","created_at":"2026-09-05T03:22:24Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":2}],"schema_version":"1.1","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["The EPA argues the case belongs in D.C. to prevent conflicting rules. The refinery argues the case belongs locally because the denial targets its specific economic harm."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 110, lines 29-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 110, lines 29-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 50, lines 29-33","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 50, lines 29-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 35-37","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 35-37"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 72, lines 27-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 72, lines 27-21"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on March 25, 2025."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 11-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 11-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 81, lines 17-53","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 81, lines 17-53"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["The EPA wants the case to stay in D.C. to ensure uniform national rules.","The refinery wants the case to remain in its local court to challenge its specific denial."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 110, lines 29-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 110, lines 29-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 50, lines 29-33","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 50, lines 29-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 35-37","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 35-37"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 72, lines 27-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 72, lines 27-21"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["The EPA argues Section 307(b) requires D.C. venue to avoid inconsistent rules from duplicative litigation.","The refinery argues the statute requires a local venue because the denial targets its specific economic harm."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 110, lines 29-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 110, lines 29-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-19"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 50, lines 29-33","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 50, lines 29-33"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 35-37","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 35-37"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 72, lines 27-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 72, lines 27-21"}]},{"heading":"What the justices asked","paragraphs":["Justice Gorsuch asked how far back a party must trace the reasoning to determine the correct venue.","Justice Thomas asked if there are limits to aggregating different claims to determine D.C. venue."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10, lines 41-45","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 10, lines 41-45"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10, lines 9-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 10, lines 9-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 25-45","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 25-45"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 55-41","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 55-41"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 6, lines 21-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2024/23-1229_3eah.pdf","page_label":"file page 6, lines 21-25"},{"evidence_type":"Tran